The reclassification is consistent with the operational semantics: `#while` normally expands and executes its condition/body, `append` mutates the heap list, `%` uses `pyMod`, and augmented assignment updates the active scope. The two priority-40 rules replace that execution with summarized state changes, so they are neither ordinary operational rules nor definitions. Their Stage 1 claims are narrower than the reusable rules (notably `builtinsScope` versus arbitrary `BI:Map` and explicit versus omitted cells), so they also fail the exact-statement requirement for `PROVED_DERIVED_LEMMA`; `DOMAIN_LEMMA` is the correct category. Both are directly relevant to the nested loops and `primesAcc` postcondition.

